{"id":"fast_aero","compound_name":"Graphs::Aero::fast_aero","source_path":"fast_aero/fast_aero.json","category":"Smoke","author":"Autodesk","description":"An aero simulation tailored for maximum performance","documentation_file":"fast_aero_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## Fast Aero\n\n### What it does\n\nAn example aero simulation tailored to maximize performance.\n\n### Inputs and outputs \n\nInputs are the sourcing geometry and the output the resulting aero volume.\n\n### Useful information\n\n  - The purpose of this example is to showcase the settings required to maximize performance to the fullest for an aero simulation. \n  - The primary performance driver is always the `Fluid Detail Size` on the `source_air`. Set it as high as the desired quality will permit.\n  - Using a low `Geometry Detail Size` on the `source_air` can also computationally expensive. Set it equal to or higher than the `Fluid Detail Size`.\n  - On the `aero_solver_settings`, the `Style` is set to `smooth` (linear). `Enhanced Accuracy` (second order time integration) has been turned off. Finally, the `Max Steps` is set to 1. These settings will ensure maximum performance, with a quality tradeoff.\n  - For faster interactive playback, the `Geometry Depth Test` and `Precompute Lighting` are disabled on the `set_viewport_volume_settings`. When interactively tumbling the camera it is an advantage to enable `Precompute Lighting`. For correct blending with surface geometry, `Geometry Depth Test` should be enabled.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","fluids":"2.15.0.9","geometries":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"source_geo","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"true"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"true"}],"counts":{"nodes":14,"connections":15,"values":82,"compounds":2},"node_types":{"Modeling::Primitive::cr